From 67061cb9acc04d47051dedd519e284a9926c32bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 52/76] v2 teardown: unlink PLE shared-memory names and the
 PLE-owned ipc socket on graceful shutdown

Baseline boots (record flashnext-v2-teardown-leak-baseline-2026-09-14) show the frozen fork
d7755c6c and the RC 3f1572af95 both leave 7 /dev/shm/torch_<pid>_* names (the connector's
share_memory_() tensors shared to the offload child under the file_system strategy) and the
PLE registration ipc socket after a clean SIGINT stop; the leak is inherited, not a v2 change.

connector.py: release_host_storage() unlinks the shm names of the seven filename-shared CPU
storages while keeping tensors, mappings and CUDA registrations alive; close() calls it last,
after request-thread join, ZMQ teardown and progress close; the deferred branch (thread did not
stop) does not unlink. worker.py: the offload child unlinks the ipc endpoint it bound after
socket close + context term; PleOffloadWorkerHandle keeps ipc_addr and unlinks as a fallback
after a confirmed child exit (SIGKILLed child). Non-graceful paths (fatal os._exit, SIGKILL,
PDEATHSIG) leak by design. The 17 upstream VLLM_RPC_BASE_PATH uuid sockets per boot are out
of scope (launch profile uses a per-boot tmpdir).

Tests: tests/v1/ple_offload/test_shm_unlink.py, test_shutdown_order.py (extended),
test_ipc_socket_unlink.py - red on 3f1572af95 (7 failed / 2 passed), green 9/9; full
tests/v1/ple_offload 135 passed / 1 skipped (logs <maintainer log path>).
Sol draft (sol-shm-fix), Fable applied/tested.
